    "summary": "Explosive Playin' sandwich lifts a shaky first set",
    "blurb": "The second set erupts with a fiery Playing In The Band > Uncle John's Band > Morning Dew jam sandwich, showcasing Jerry's raging guitar and Keith's soaring keys. First‑set material is uneven, with the Weather Report Suite flailing, but highlights like Jack Straw and Big River keep the momentum.",
    "review": "Winterland, November 10 1973, finds the Dead in a classic late‑'73 swing. The first set meanders through a solid Bertha and an energetic Jack Straw before sagging on the Weather Report Suite and some lackluster moments like Loser. The real magic ignites in the second set when the band launches into a pressure‑cooker Playin' > Uncle John's Band > Morning Dew sandwich that rolls back into Playin' again, delivering one of the season’s most memorable jams. Jerry Garcia is on fire, his guitar swirls and riffs driving the intensity, while Keith Godchaux adds cascading keyboard textures during Wharf Rat. Big River and Stella Blue provide soulful contrast before a tight Truckin'/Wharf Rat/Sugar Magnolia run closes the set. The show ends with the usual Saturday Night crowd‑pleasers, One More Saturday Night and Casey Jones.\n\nTwo soundboard sources exist: one suffers from pitch and speed issues but captures the second‑set fireworks, while the Miller‑Clugston recording offers crystal‑clear fidelity that lets every note shine. For most listeners the latter is the preferred pick, delivering a pristine listening experience without compromising the performance’s power.",
